── NOTES ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
1. RUN B is the authoritative flow and produced ui-1-drawer-before.png,
   ui-2-confirm.png, ui-3-after-delete-list.png: labeled danger button
   ("btn btn--danger-outline btn--sm cus-container-row__remove") → confirm
   "Xóa container QATU0001234?" with removePosts=0 BEFORE confirm → POST
   …/containers/141260/remove → 200 → drawer CLOSED → toast "Đã xóa container
   QATU0001234". ui-3 shows the refreshed list with the drawer closed, the
   success toast, and the cont search now returning "Không có lô hàng phù
   hợp" — the deleted cont is GONE from the list (the ROW-AFTER wait expected
   a 1-row chip change and timed out; the 0-row outcome is the correct
   "danh sách mất cont" for a cont-term search — the driver was updated to
   accept it).
2. ui-4-drawer-after-reopen.png comes from RUN A's read-only re-open
   (09:44, same build): drawer head "1 cont", deleted cont absent, survivor
   present, chip 1x20DC. db-before.txt/db-after.txt bracket RUN B's delete
   (141260 removed by hard delete, shipments.version 2→3).
3. Lot 311985 is a QA-seed fixture on the SHARED dev DB — another lane
   re-seeded it at 09:52 (new container ids 141259/141260). RUN A's delete
   (141231) and RUN B's delete (141260) are both genuine API deletes; the
   restore attempt via the add API failed by design (ISO-6340 check-digit
   validator — the seed bypasses it), so the lot rests at 1 cont.
4. 390 attempt 1 raced the filter debounce and clicked the wrong lot (0
   conts); attempt 2 waited for exactly 1 row and asserts the real contract:
   label "Xóa container", visible, height 40 (touch floor = ceiling), inside
   the 390px viewport → ui-5-drawer-390.png.
5. Environment: local dev — frontend vite :7185 (THIS worktree, CUS-10
   build), backend :3012 (this worktree) → Postgres ss-prod-db :5441/silversea
   (shared dev DB). Account: cus (CUS role). Lot 311985
   (QA-QAENV01-FCL-KEP, fixture, PENDING_DATE, FCL, no trips).
